# Supabase Configuration
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-supabase-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your_supabase_anon_key_here
VITE_PUBLIC_AGENCY_SLUG=dream-supreme-properties

# Document storage bucket name, used client-side only to display which bucket is
# active (see Admin > Settings). Direct client-side Cloudflare R2 access is
# impossible — Vite inlines every VITE_-prefixed value into the shipped browser
# bundle, so an R2 IAM secret key can never be safely stored under a VITE_ variable.
# Real uploads/downloads instead go through the `r2-storage` Supabase Edge Function
# (supabase/functions/r2-storage), which holds the R2 credentials as server-side
# secrets and hands the browser short-lived presigned URLs. Set those secrets with:
#   supabase secrets set R2_ACCOUNT_ID=... R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=... \
#     R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=... R2_BUCKET_NAME=dream-supreme-documents
# then deploy with `supabase functions deploy r2-storage`. Until those secrets are
# set, storage transparently falls back to Supabase Storage.
VITE_R2_BUCKET_NAME=dream-supreme-documents

# Restricts the admin portal UI to this hostname/origin (see src/lib/auth-routing.ts).
VITE_ADMIN_DOMAIN=admin.yourdomain.com

# Integration status flag shown on Admin > Settings. Only ever checked for truthy
# presence to render a "Connected / Not configured" badge — never read as a real
# credential. Do not put a real API token/secret in a VITE_-prefixed variable; if this
# integration starts making authenticated calls, move that call server-side first
# (same reasoning as the R2 credential above).
VITE_CONVEYANCER_WEBHOOK_URL=https://your-webhook-endpoint.example.com
